decision: changes-requested

All five prior findings are fixed. Two additional medium blockers remain in Markdown association parsing.

The focused closeout-policy tests passed across domain, CLI, and MCP packages. The round-twelve and round-thirteen regressions also passed without skips. The worktree remains unchanged.

Prior findings:

| Finding | Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| R11-N39 | fixed | `associationList` preserves presence and rejects empty items and duplicates; round-twelve regressions passed. |
| R12-N42 | fixed | `approvedBeforeAdoption` checks the sealed plan; both history regressions passed. |
| R12-N43 | fixed | Both templates declare `adrs: []`; template regression passed. |
| R12-N44 | fixed | Fence character and length are preserved; longer-fence regression passed. |
| R12-N45 | fixed | Keys are trimmed and values cleaned before duplicate detection; normalization regressions passed. |

New blockers:

- **N46 — medium**, [closeout_adr_associations.go:92](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3650767735/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:92): Code filtering can discard real association links. An indented code line containing `~~~` is treated as a fence opener and suppresses subsequent prose. Comment removal also crosses fenced-code boundaries.
- **N47 — medium**, [closeout_adr_associations.go:33](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3650767735/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go:33): Balanced parentheses in a valid link destination truncate the parsed ADR filename. Both defects can incorrectly exempt a two-member roadmap under `when-justified`.

Rules applied: mixed Go feature and governance change; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules.

